<title>JAPAN: Minolta to boost printer toner production capacity.</title>
<headline>Minolta to boost printer toner production capacity.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese camera maker Minolta Co Ltd said on Monday that it has begun constructing a new facility in Kobe to make toner for copiers and printers in response to growing demand.</p>
<p>The facility will start operating in November, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company plans total capital spending of about 4.3 billion yen in the printer toner business during the two-year period from April 1997 to March 1999, it said.</p>
</text>
